>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (          In the present digital era, technology has become an essential part of education, employment, and professional development. The rapid advancement of software technologies has resulted in the continuous creation of new job roles and career opportunities. At the same time, the skills required for existing job roles are also changing regularly. As a result, students, graduates, and job seekers need to continuously improve their knowledge and technical skills to meet the requirements of their desired career. However, many individuals are not fully aware of the skills they already possess, the skills required for a particular career, or the specific areas in which they need improvement.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
520 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (          Choosing a suitable career is an important decision for students and job seekers. A career decision generally depends on several factors, including educational qualification, interests, existing knowledge, technical skills, and future career goals. Without proper guidance, individuals may select a career without understanding its actual skill requirements. This can result in a mismatch between their current capabilities and the expectations associated with the selected career. Identifying this mismatch at an early stage can help individuals plan their learning activities more effectively.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
521 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (          A skill gap refers to the difference between the skills currently possessed by an individual and the skills required for a particular career role. For example, a person interested in becoming a Web Developer may already have knowledge of HTML, but may require additional knowledge of CSS, JavaScript, databases, or other relevant technologies. Understanding such differences allows the individual to focus on the areas that require improvement rather than spending unnecessary time learning skills that are already known.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (          The application begins with a user authentication process. After successful login, the user can provide relevant profile information such as personal and educational details. The user can then select a preferred career role from the available career options. The selected career role acts as the basis for the subsequent skill analysis process.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (          Once the career role is selected, the system identifies the skills associated with that role and compares them with the user's current skills. The skills that are present in both sets are treated as matched skills, while the required skills that are not available in the user's current skill set are identified as missing skills. The system also calculates a skill match percentage to provide a simple numerical representation of the user's current alignment with the selected career requirements.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 330 0 R
/T (I. INTRODUCTION)
/E (I. INTRODUCTION)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (Skill Gap Analysis and Personalized Roadmap)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
527 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 330 0 R
/E (1)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          The results of the analysis are presented through a dedicated Skill Gap page. This page allows the user to understand the relationship between their existing skills and the expected skills for the selected career. Instead of providing only a general career recommendation, the system gives specific information about what the user already knows and what needs to be learned.)
/E (          The results of the analysis are presented through a dedicated Skill Gap page. This page allows the user to understand the relationship between their existing skills and the expected skills for the selected career. Instead of providing only a general career recommendation, the system gives specific information about what the user already knows and what needs to be learned.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          One of the important features of the proposed system is the Personalized Roadmap Generator. The roadmap is generated according to the user's selected career and identified skill gaps. The system focuses on missing skills rather than providing a generic learning sequence. Each roadmap item can provide access to external learning resources related to the particular skill. This approach allows users to follow a more focused learning path based on their individual requirements.)
/E (          One of the important features of the proposed system is the Personalized Roadmap Generator. The roadmap is generated according to the user's selected career and identified skill gaps. The system focuses on missing skills rather than providing a generic learning sequence. Each roadmap item can provide access to external learning resources related to the particular skill. This approach allows users to follow a more focused learning path based on their individual requirements.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
530 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          The system also generates a Career Report that summarizes the user's analysis results. The report can contain details such as the selected career role, current skills, required skills, matched skills, missing skills, and skill match percentage. This summary helps users review their current position and understand the areas that require further development.)
/E (          The system also generates a Career Report that summarizes the user's analysis results. The report can contain details such as the selected career role, current skills, required skills, matched skills, missing skills, and skill match percentage. This summary helps users review their current position and understand the areas that require further development.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
531 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          The application is implemented using modern web development technologies. Python with Flask is used to develop the backend and handle application routes and processing logic. MySQL is used for storing user information, profile details, career selections, and analysis-related data. HTML and CSS are used to develop the web pages and provide a user-friendly interface. A career-skill dataset is used to associate different career roles with their required technical skills.)
/E (          The application is implemented using modern web development technologies. Python with Flask is used to develop the backend and handle application routes and processing logic. MySQL is used for storing user information, profile details, career selections, and analysis-related data. HTML and CSS are used to develop the web pages and provide a user-friendly interface. A career-skill dataset is used to associate different career roles with their required technical skills.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
532 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          The system follows a modular approach so that each major function can be developed and maintained independently. The major modules include User Login, Profile Management, Career Selection, Skill Gap Analysis, Skill Matching, Personalized Roadmap, and Career Report. These modules are connected to provide a complete flow from user registration/login to skill analysis and personalized learning guidance.)
/E (          The system follows a modular approach so that each major function can be developed and maintained independently. The major modules include User Login, Profile Management, Career Selection, Skill Gap Analysis, Skill Matching, Personalized Roadmap, and Career Report. These modules are connected to provide a complete flow from user registration/login to skill analysis and personalized learning guidance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
533 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          The main purpose of the project is not only to identify a user's skill gap but also to transform the analysis into an actionable learning plan. By connecting skill analysis with a personalized roadmap, the system provides users with a clearer understanding of their learning requirements. This can reduce confusion during career preparation and help users concentrate on relevant skills.)
/E (          The main purpose of the project is not only to identify a user's skill gap but also to transform the analysis into an actionable learning plan. By connecting skill analysis with a personalized roadmap, the system provides users with a clearer understanding of their learning requirements. This can reduce confusion during career preparation and help users concentrate on relevant skills.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 331 0 R
/T (          Overall, the Skill Gap Analysis & Personalized Roadmap Generator provides a structured approach to career- oriented skill development. It combines user information, career requirements, skill comparison, and roadmap generation into a single web-based platform. The system demonstrates how software technologies can be used to support individuals in understanding their skill requirements and planning their learning journey in a systematic manner.)
/E (          Overall, the Skill Gap Analysis & Personalized Roadmap Generator provides a structured approach to career- oriented skill development. It combines user information, career requirements, skill comparison, and roadmap generation into a single web-based platform. The system demonstrates how software technologies can be used to support individuals in understanding their skill requirements and planning their learning journey in a systematic manner.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
