619 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (           Career selection and skill development are important activities for students, graduates, and job seekers. In the existing environment, individuals generally depend on different sources such as general career guidance websites, online learning platforms, search engines, educational resources, social media content, and advice from teachers or professionals to understand career opportunities and skill requirements. Although these resources provide useful information, they are often separated from one another and may not provide a complete picture of an individual's current skill level.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
620 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (          Traditional career guidance methods generally begin with identifying a career based on a person's interests, educational qualification, or general understanding of the job market. Once a career is selected, the individual has to independently search for the skills required for that career. The user then needs to compare those requirements with their own knowledge and skills. This process requires considerable effort because information about career requirements, skill lists, and learning resources is usually available across different platforms.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
621 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (          In many existing systems, career recommendations are provided as general suggestions. A user may receive information about different career roles and their descriptions, but the system may not necessarily analyze the user's current technical skills in detail. As a result, the user may know which career they are interested in but may not clearly understand which skills they already possess and which skills they still need to develop.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
622 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (          Another common approach is the use of online skill assessment platforms. Such systems may provide quizzes, tests, or assessments to measure a user's knowledge in a particular technical area. The results can indicate the user's performance in the selected assessment. However, assessment results alone may not provide a complete career-oriented learning path. The user may still need to identify the relationship between the assessment result and the skills required for a particular career.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
623 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 338 0 R
/E (          Online learning platforms provide another source of career development information. These platforms offer courses and tutorials covering programming languages, web development, databases, data analysis, and other technical areas. However, most learning platforms are designed primarily for course delivery rather than personalized career skill-gap analysis. Users are generally required to decide what they should learn and in what order.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
