1813 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          The SKILL GAP ANALYSIS & PERSONALIZED ROADMAP GENERATOR is a web-based career guidance application developed to help users understand the skills required for a selected career and identify the difference between their existing skills and the skills expected for that career. The system provides an organized approach to career-oriented skill analysis by bringing profile management, career selection, skill comparison, roadmap generation, and career reporting into a single application.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
1814 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          In the existing approach, users often depend on different websites, learning platforms, search engines, and manual comparisons to understand the skills required for a particular career. This process can require considerable effort and may make it difficult for beginners to determine which skills they should learn first. The proposed system addresses this problem by providing a structured workflow from career selection to skill-gap identification and personalized learning guidance.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1815 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          The application begins with user authentication. After successful login, the user can manage their profile and select a preferred career role. The selected career is associated with the required skills available in the career- skill dataset. The system then considers the user's current skills and compares them with the required skills for the selected career.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1816 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          The Skill Gap Analysis Module is an important component of the application. It identifies the skills that the user already possesses and the skills that are missing for the selected career. The system also calculates a skill matching percentage, providing the user with a simple numerical representation of the relationship between their current skills and the required skills.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1817 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          The Skill Matching Module further organizes the comparison by presenting matched and missing skills. This makes it easier for users to understand their current position with respect to their selected career. Instead of requiring users to manually compare multiple skill lists, the application performs the comparison automatically.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1818 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          One of the major features of the project is the Personalized Roadmap Module. The roadmap is generated using the skill-gap information obtained from the analysis. The identified missing skills are converted into learning steps so that users can focus on the areas where additional learning is required. Relevant external learning resources can also be accessed through the roadmap, allowing users to continue their learning outside the application.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1819 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (          The Career Report Module provides an organized summary of the user's career and skill analysis information. It allows the user to view the important results in a consolidated format. The report can help users understand their selected career, current skills, required skills, matched skills, and identified skill gaps.)
/Pg 82 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
