/Title (For example, consider a student who wants to become a Web Developer. The student may first search for the skills required for web development. The student may then prepare a list of technologies such as HTML, CSS, JavaScript, database concepts, and other relevant skills. After that, the student must compare this list with the skills they already know. If the student identifies missing skills, another search is required to find appropriate learning resources. Finally, the student must create a learning sequence manually.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 4319 0 R
/Next 4323 0 R
>>
